text She moves away from the window and sits back down right next to me.
text @[Tomoya]
text Mommy seemed like she was always crying.
text @[Tomoya]
text When I first met her, she didn't have any confidence, and she was weak... She was always standing, paralyzed at the bottom of this steep hill that led up to our school.
text @[Tomoya]
text And guess what she said down at the bottom of that hill?
text @[Tomoya]
text She had her eyes closed as she said "anpan."
text @[Tomoya]
text It was a funny habit of hers.
text @[Tomoya]
text She'd say the name of something she wanted to eat in order to get herself to climb the hill. It was what she did to give herself courage...
text @[Tomoya]
text Isn't that such a cute habit...? I mean, she was being so modest...
text @[Tomoya]
text There was a lot of competition for the bread at our school, you see... And it was hard to get the most popular kinds...
music ~
text @[Tomoya]
text So she'd use anpan, the one thing that was always left over, to cheer herself up...
text @[Tomoya]
text But she stopped doing that after she and I started going out.
text @[Tomoya]
text She started using me to support her.
text @[Tomoya]
text And she supported me back.
music BGM32B.mp3
text @[Tomoya]
text Together, we helped each other through our time in school.
