text I've worked up the courage to force myself to stand in the doorway.
text ...Nagisa's room.
text The room has been cleaned up, but it's exactly as it was back then.
text I gather into my arms the stuffed dango that I had them hold on to ever since that day.
text Then, I bury my face in them.
text Is this what Nagisa smelled like...?
text Back in those days, so long ago...
text I feel like I could travel back to that time if only I close my eyes.
text The time when Nagisa was by my side.
text But I don't want to see that kind of dream any longer.
text That would mean leaving Ushio behind.
text I need to face reality head-on...
text So I leave my eyes open... and feel the time that's gone by pass into me like a spreading pain.
