music BGM08D.mp3
text The next morning.
text I'm woken up by the old man's screams and shouts as he prepares to open the store.
text Ushio is asleep, wrapped up in her blanket.
text She looks just like an angel in the morning light.
text @[Tomoya]
text (Look at me, acting like a doting father...)
text I let out a puff of laughter, then begin to think of what to do next.
text Life with Ushio.
text It'll probably be harder than I imagine.
text But Sanae-san looked after her during the most difficult period of them all.
text Whatever hardships lay ahead for me, nothing will compare to that.
text When I think about it that way, I kind of feel like I'll be able to deal with any problems that come up.
text And anyway, while there may be tough times ahead, there'll surely be even more great times too.
text That's what it means to live as a family.
text As someone who lived with the person they loved... I've experienced that for myself more than anyone else I can imagine.
text But before I start life with Ushio, there's a promise I have to fulfill first.
text As far as work goes, I'll ask for just one more day off.
text And that's when I'll make good on that promise.
text I leave the room with Ushio still asleep.
